# AI and development files (don't deploy to production)
AI_PROJECT_GUIDE.md
*.md

# Project methodology — track these despite the broad *.md rule above.
# (Vite already excludes .md from the production bundle, so the *.md gitignore
# was over-broad. These files belong in version control so they survive a
# fresh clone / laptop reset.)
#
# Specific paths only — adding `*.md` globs here would pull in pre-existing
# documentation files (e.g. tests_evm/CONTRACT_ANALYSIS.md) that the dev had
# kept local-only. Add new exemptions explicitly as new methodology files
# are created.
# INTERNAL — deliberately NOT tracked since the repo went public (2026-07-30).
# BRAIN.md / TODO.md / tech_learnings.md / workflow_rules.md / memory/ / notes/
# are planning and status documents. They record infrastructure detail, key-store
# layout, incident history and machine-local paths — a disclosure surface, not
# product code. They stay on disk; they do not ship. Do NOT re-add an exemption
# for them without re-reading what is actually inside first.
#   -> they are therefore covered by the broad `*.md` rule above, plus:
memory/
notes/
bugs/

# README is the repo's front page — it was tracked before the clean-repo rebuild
# (2026-07-30) and the broad *.md rule above would silently drop it on re-add.
!README.md
!tests_evm/BANK8_VERIFICATION_*.md
!tools/contract-debug/README.md
!tools/hardhat-deploy/_WHAT_THIS_IS.md
!docs/*.md
!docs/grants/*.md
!docs/screenshots/*.md
# Playwright MCP snapshot artifacts
.playwright-mcp/

# Local deploy config — names the machine-local pass entry, never publish
tools/hardhat-deploy/.deploy-local

# Pool E2E preimage — local test artifact, never publish
.pool-e2e-preimage.local

# Anchor build artifacts
contracts/solana/target/
contracts/solana/.anchor/
